  "interpretation": [
    "None of the twelve final retained versions passed the entire private suite. There was no private-perfect alternative for a better selector to recover in these three pools.",
    "Only four of the twelve final versions passed all active public/probe checks with valid source. All twelve had empty recorded reviewer_remaining lists; empty lists on unselected slots are not evidence that a reviewer individually accepted them.",
    "Calendar repetition1 has a limited partial opportunity: eligible B failed4 private cases versus selected D5, but both cover11/15 requirements. Their union covers12/15 requirements, combining different implementations and not constituting an executable release.",
    "Every final pool has at least one private case failed by all four sources. Shared failing cases are observations, not counts of independent root-cause defects.",
    "Three earlier portfolio stops remain end-to-end completion failures; no final pools existed for them. The final-pool findings are conditional on the three survivors.",
    "Each milestone starts all four builders from the same prior selected repository, notes/history and retained probes. Only one lineage survives between milestones. Two selected final versions also received a repair while their peers did not.",
    "Common failures are consistent with inherited errors or shared specification/model/evidence blind spots; final overlap cannot isolate their cause. More reliable verification and persistence deserve priority over selector tuning or simply adding similar candidates under this tested architecture."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic fixtures and three reached final pools do not establish a general result about swarm architectures.",
    "This is a post-hoc final-pool diagnostic after unequal repairs, not initial independent best-of-four, not twelve independent projects, and not a new acceptance test.",
    "Private evidence was used only after the entire study froze and cannot be fed back into these runs."
  ],
